Install the llmapi-audit Skill (version 0.1.0, darwin-arm64) for your agent, so that you can query the LLM API audit server at https://audit.example.com through its command-line client llmaudit.

Rules for this whole task:
- Execute the numbered steps below in order, one at a time, running each command exactly as written. Do not skip, merge or reorder steps.
- If a command fails or a step's check does not hold, stop at once. Do not try to repair it and do not continue with later steps. Tell the user which step failed and show the exact output.
- Use only the download link in this prompt. Never fetch the package from any other address, mirror or repository, and never switch to another install method (a package manager, a git clone, building from source, copying files by hand).
- Change nothing outside the install directory /Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit. Never delete or modify its parent directory /Users/example/agent-skills or anything else in it. The one exception is the temporary work directory LLMAPI_WORK_DIR (the private directory step 1 creates with mktemp), which this prompt creates and removes.
- Nothing here asks for a password, an API key or a token, and you must not ask the user for one. The login in a later step is authorized by the user in the browser.
- Run the commands in a POSIX shell (sh, bash or zsh). Every command is complete on its own; nothing depends on shell variables from an earlier step. The one value carried from step to step is the work directory path that step 1 prints: write it in place of LLMAPI_WORK_DIR in every later command, inside the double quotes as shown.

Final install directory: /Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit
Package file: llmapi-audit-0.1.0-darwin-arm64.zip (3456789 bytes)
Expected SHA-256: 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
The download link is valid until 2026-01-02T03:34:05Z. HTTP 410 (Gone) means it has expired: stop and ask the user to generate a new install prompt on the Agent access page of the web UI. HTTP 404 means the link or file is not valid: stop and report it.
The archive's top level is the directory llmapi-audit/ itself: it contains llmapi-audit/SKILL.md, llmapi-audit/VERSION, llmapi-audit/references/ and llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit. It is extracted into a work directory and then moved to the install directory as a whole, so it is never nested twice.

1. Create a private work directory with a random name:
   mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/llmapi-audit-install.XXXXXXXX"
   Check: the command exits with status 0 and prints one absolute path made only of letters, digits and the characters / . _ -. If nothing is printed or the path has any other character (a space, for example), stop.
   From now on write that exact path wherever a command says LLMAPI_WORK_DIR. Never run a command that still contains LLMAPI_WORK_DIR itself.

2. Download the package from the link in this prompt, and only from it:
   curl -fsS --max-redirs 0 -o "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/llmapi-audit-0.1.0-darwin-arm64.zip" "https://audit.example.com/api/agent/v1/dl/MTc2NzMyNjI0NS5leGFtcGxlLXNpZ25hdHVyZQ/llmapi-audit-0.1.0-darwin-arm64.zip"
   Check: the command exits with status 0. If curl reports HTTP 410, the link has expired; if it reports another error, stop either way.

3. Verify the SHA-256 digest of the download:
   shasum -a 256 "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/llmapi-audit-0.1.0-darwin-arm64.zip"
   Check: the first field printed is exactly 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef. If it differs in any character, stop: do not extract or run the file, and tell the user the digest did not match.

4. Extract the archive into the work directory:
   unzip -q "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/llmapi-audit-0.1.0-darwin-arm64.zip" -d "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/extract"
   If unzip is not installed, run this instead: python3 -m zipfile -e "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/llmapi-audit-0.1.0-darwin-arm64.zip" "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/extract"
   If neither unzip nor python3 is available, stop and ask the user to install unzip.
   Then run: ls -A "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/extract" && ls "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/extract/llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit"
   Check: the first listing shows exactly one entry, llmapi-audit, and the second command finds the file.

5. Check what is at the install directory now:
   if [ -L "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit" ]; then echo foreign; ls -la "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit"; elif [ ! -e "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit" ]; then echo absent; elif [ -f "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit" ]; then echo previous-install; else echo foreign; ls -la "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit"; fi
   - absent: nothing is there; continue with the next step.
   - previous-install: it is an earlier install of this Skill (it contains scripts/llmaudit). Remove that directory, and only it:
     rm -rf -- "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit"
   - foreign: something else is there. Stop. Delete nothing, and show the user the listing so they can decide what to do.

6. Move the extracted Skill into place (the skills directory is created if it does not exist; nothing else in it is touched):
   mkdir -p -- "/Users/example/agent-skills" && [ ! -e "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit" ] && mv -- "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR/extract/llmapi-audit" "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit" && chmod 755 "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit"
   Check: the command exits with status 0.

7. Remove the work directory:
   rm -rf -- "LLMAPI_WORK_DIR"

8. Check that the client runs on this machine:
   "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit" --help
   Check: it exits with status 0 and prints the usage of llmaudit.

9. Log in. The user authorizes this machine in the browser:
   "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit" login --server "https://audit.example.com"
   The command opens the server's authorization page in the browser and waits up to 5 minutes while the user signs in there and approves. It never asks for a password, an API key or a token, and you must not ask the user for any of them.
   If your environment cannot open a browser or cannot keep a command running that long, ask the user to run this exact command themselves in a terminal and to tell you when it has finished. Adding --no-browser makes it print an address the user can open in any browser; the page then shows a one-time code that the user types into the terminal themselves.
   Check: the command exits successfully. If it reports LOGIN_TIMEOUT or LOGIN_DENIED, stop and tell the user.

10. Verify the login:
   "/Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit/scripts/llmaudit" whoami
   Check: the output is one JSON object with "ok":true. Note data.role, data.tier and data.expires_at for your report.

When every step has succeeded, tell the user: the llmapi-audit Skill is installed in /Users/example/agent-skills/llmapi-audit, the role and tier that whoami reported, and that your agent should be started in a new session (or have its skills reloaded) before the Skill is available, because agents load skills when a session starts.
